<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ data.title }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --accent: #1f5f8b; --rule: #d0d0d0; --muted: #666666; }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #222; margin: 0 auto;
         max-width: 1200px; padding: 16px 24px; line-height: 1.45; font-size: 14px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 3px;
       margin-top: 32px; }
  h3 { font-size: 14px; margin: 16px 0 6px 0; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .meta span { margin-right: 18px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12px; margin: 8px 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 2px 6px; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; }
  th { background: #f4f4f4; font-weight: 600; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; }
  details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); margin: 6px 0; }
  code, pre { font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12px; }
  pre { background: #f7f7f7; border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap;
        word-break: break-all; }
  figure { margin: 12px 0; }
  figure svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  figcaption { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .methods { max-width: 900px; text-align: justify; }
  ul.failures li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  @media print { details { display: block; } details > *:not(summary) { display: block; }
                 h2 { page-break-after: avoid; } table, figure { page-break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>{{ data.title }}</h1>
<p class="meta">
  <span>generated {{ generated }}</span>
  <span>mlvatyper {{ version }}</span>
  <span>merPCR {{ merpcr_version }}</span>
  <span>{{ data.samples | length }} samples</span>
  <span>{{ data.markers | length }} markers</span>
  <span>{{ data.n_amplicons }} amplicons</span>
</p>
<pre>{{ command }}</pre>

<h2>1. Summary</h2>
<p>Status codes per sample. OK counts markers with an amplicon and an allele within tolerance of an integer;
the other codes are explained in the glossary at the end.</p>
<div class="scroll">{{ counts_table | safe }}</div>
{% if failures %}
<ul class="failures">
{% for code, explanation, items in failures %}
  <li><strong>{{ code }}</strong> ({{ items | length }}): {{ explanation }}.
      <span class="meta">{{ items[:12] | join(", ") }}{% if items | length > 12 %}, ...{% endif %}</span></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p>Every marker was found in every sample without flags.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>2. Allele profiles</h2>
<p>Alleles as repeat numbers in STS order; several amplicons for one marker are joined with a slash. Cells are
shaded by their status code. The profile string per sample is the input format for MLVAbank.</p>
<div class="scroll">{{ alleles_table | safe }}</div>
<details><summary>Profile strings</summary><div class="scroll">{{ profile_table | safe }}</div></details>

<h2>3. Figures</h2>
<figure>{{ data.figures.lengths | safe }}
<figcaption>Amplicon length per marker (points) and the expected size from the STS file (grey tick).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>{{ data.figures.residuals | safe }}
<figcaption>Residual between the amplicon length and the expected size of the called allele. Values other than
zero indicate flanking indels, primer indels or a wrong unit length.</figcaption></figure>
<figure>{{ data.figures.status | safe }}
<figcaption>Status per sample and marker: white OK, grey missing, yellow several or ambiguous loci, orange
intermediate repeat number or count disagreement, blue primer indel or N, red outside the bin table or
censored.</figcaption></figure>

<h2>4. Evidence per amplicon</h2>
<p>One row per amplicon: coordinates, length, expected size, residual, primer mismatches and indels, the search
pass that found it (main, rescue, aligned), the allele and the tandem array count with exact and variant
windows.</p>
{% for sample in data.samples %}
<details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}><summary>{{ sample }}</summary>
<div class="scroll">{{ evidence[sample] | safe }}</div></details>
{% endfor %}

<h2>5. Markers without amplicon</h2>
{% if missing_table %}
<div class="scroll">{{ missing_table | safe }}</div>
{% else %}
<p>None.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if discovery_table %}
<h2>6. Repeat unit discovery</h2>
<p>Primary candidate per marker from <code>mlvatyper discover</code>, with its category (A strong, B plausible,
C weak), the number of candidates, the mixed flag and the cross-sample evidence when several samples were used.</p>
<details><summary>Discovery report</summary><div class="scroll">{{ discovery_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% endif %}

<h2>{{ "7" if discovery_table else "6" }}. Methods</h2>
<p class="methods">{{ methods }}</p>
{% if inputs %}
<h3>Input files</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>file</th><th>size (bytes)</th><th>MD5</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for item in inputs %}
<tr><td>{{ item.path }}</td><td>{{ item.size }}</td><td><code>{{ item.md5 }}</code></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% endif %}
<details><summary>Recorded parameters (run_info.json)</summary><pre>{{ parameters }}</pre></details>

<h2>{{ "8" if discovery_table else "7" }}. Appendix</h2>
{% if definitions_table %}
<h3>Marker definitions used</h3>
<details><summary>Definitions</summary><div class="scroll">{{ definitions_table | safe }}</div></details>
{% endif %}
<h3>Status codes</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>code</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for code, meaning in glossary.items() %}
<tr><td>{{ code }}</td><td>{{ meaning }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>

</body>
</html>
